      "title": "Read me first",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 12 - An instrumental\n\nMusic with no voice in it. YuE2 on its own sings whatever the style says --\n\"instrumental\" or \"no vocals\" in the style does not stop it -- so this\ntemplate puts Mothersuperior's instrumental adapter in front of the song\nnode. It was trained on instrumental tracks and writes a score with no notes\nfor the voice, and then plays that score.\n\n## What it needs\n\n- The YuE2-3B weights, 7.26 GB, fetched on the first run.\n- The adapter, which this pack never downloads:\n  `ar_lora_inst_v3abc.safetensors`, 279 MB, from\n  https://huggingface.co/Mothersuperior/YuE2-instrumental-cot-full-loras\n  Put it anywhere under ComfyUI's `models/loras`: the row finds a file by\n  its name in any folder there. It is CC BY-NC 4.0, like YuE2 itself --\n  non-commercial use only.\n- `ar_lora_inst_v3abc_comfyui.safetensors` from the same page works as\n  well; choose it on the row instead.\n\n## How to use it\n\n1. Describe the sound in the style: genre, instruments, mood, BPM.\n2. Leave the lyrics at `[instrumental]`, or plan the sections yourself,\n   one bare tag a line and nothing else:\n\n   ```\n   [intro]\n   [verse]\n   [chorus]\n   [bridge]\n   [chorus]\n   [outro]\n   ```\n\n   The adapter knows `intro`, `verse`, `pre-chorus`, `chorus`, `bridge` and\n   `outro`.\n3. Run. With `max_seconds` at 0 a song without words may run to 180 s;\n   the adapter likes two to three minutes and ends most songs by itself.\n\n## What makes it sing again\n\n- `cot` at anything but `full`. With `melody` the model writes a tune for\n  the voice and sings it. Keep the options node at `full`.\n- Words in the lyrics. They get sung.\n- An AR strength below 1. At 0.5 every song had a voice.\n\nThe adapter changes the AR half only, so its NAR column shows a dash.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- **10 - A song with LoRA** -- the same node with an empty list, for\n  adapters of your own.\n- **9 - An a cappella song** -- the other way round: the voice alone.\n- **11 - Edit a song** -- **Break...** puts an instrumental break into a\n  song that is sung.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# 12 - An instrumental\n\nMusic with no voice in it. YuE2 on its own sings whatever the style says --\n\"instrumental\" or \"no vocals\" in the style does not stop it -- so this\ntemplate puts Mothersuperior's instrumental adapter in front of the song\nnode. It was trained on instrumental tracks and writes a score with no notes\nfor the voice, and then plays that score.\n\n## What it needs\n\n- The YuE2-3B weights, 7.26 GB, fetched on the first run.\n- The adapter, which this pack never downloads:\n  `ar_lora_inst_v3abc.safetensors`, 279 MB, from\n  https://huggingface.co/Mothersuperior/YuE2-instrumental-cot-full-loras\n  Put it anywhere under ComfyUI's `models/loras`: the row finds a file by\n  its name in any folder there. It is CC BY-NC 4.0, like YuE2 itself --\n  non-commercial use only.\n- `ar_lora_inst_v3abc_comfyui.safetensors` from the same page works as\n  well; choose it on the row instead.\n\n## How to use it\n\n1. Describe the sound in the style: genre, instruments, mood, BPM.\n2. Leave the lyrics at `[instrumental]`, or plan the sections yourself,\n   one bare tag a line and nothing else:\n\n   ```\n   [intro]\n   [verse]\n   [chorus]\n   [bridge]\n   [chorus]\n   [outro]\n   ```\n\n   The adapter knows `intro`, `verse`, `pre-chorus`, `chorus`, `bridge` and\n   `outro`.\n3. Run. With `max_seconds` at 0 a song without words may run to 180 s;\n   the adapter likes two to three minutes and ends most songs by itself.\n\n## What makes it sing again\n\n- `cot` at anything but `full`. With `melody` the model writes a tune for\n  the voice and sings it. Keep the options node at `full`.\n- Words in the lyrics. They get sung.\n- An AR strength below 1. At 0.5 every song had a voice.\n\nThe adapter changes the AR half only, so its NAR column shows a dash.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- **10 - A song with LoRA** -- the same node with an empty list, for\n  adapters of your own.\n- **9 - An a cappella song** -- the other way round: the voice alone.\n- **11 - Edit a song** -- **Break...** puts an instrumental break into a\n  song that is sung.\n"
      },
